WEBVTT

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:28.620
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:28.620
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:28.620
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.070 --> 00:02:02.350
Chapter IX

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:07.920
On November 10th
 of Space Year 788...

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.900
...shortly after being assigned to the POW camp on Planet Econia...

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:16.360
...Lt. Commander Yang Wenli was to become involved in quelling a prison rebellion.

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:21.770
While on nighttime inspection, Vice-Superintendent Jennings and his subordinates...

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:23.670
...about 6 Alliance soldiers in total...

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:28.410
...were taken hostage
by the prisoners.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:47.410
Lt. Commander Yang !

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:54.790
Will he scold me
for being late ?

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:04.120
The 17th Compound in the
East Block has been taken over.

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:07.950
There are approximately 80 prisoners
now involved in this escape attempt...

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:12.950
...but it's possible that the
number might grow in time.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:17.850
At maximum, it'll
multiply 700 times.

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:22.070
This is terrible.

00:03:24.230 --> 00:03:29.530
At this point, it isn't necessary to beat up
only 15 prisoners with my bare knuckles.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:33.160
It'd be better to quell this rebellion, sooner rather than later, but...

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:36.700
Do you know the whereabouts of the
Shadow Emperor, Captain Kefenhiller ?

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:41.800
He might help us
persuade the escapees.

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:45.790
Kefenhiller is
in that compound.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.250
Has he been taken hostage ?

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:52.870
We can't be certain.{don't know if that's happened.}
But it's highly probable.

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:55.690
Oh well, what an
encouraging sign...

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:03.020
Lt. Commander Yang, go and investigate this situation along with Lt. Patorichev.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:27.700
Oh, dear. I'm not
good at these things.

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:37.020
I hear it's been fifty years
since the last major rebellion.

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:40.570
Looks like you've arrived
at an unfortunate time.

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:43.150
"Unfortunate time," huh ?

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:48.650
But I wonder where those escapees are
planning to go once they break out of here ?

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:53.900
They're probably planning to execute
a long march of 10,000 light years.

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:56.520
Can it actually be done ?

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:02.100
I heard that someone named Ale Heinessen
pulled it off, over 200 years ago.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:10.180
If they pull off this once every 200 years feat,
will our names be recorded in history, too ?

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:13.370
Of course, as the
incompetent "enemy" figures.

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:18.160
That's the 17th Compound
in the East Block.

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:37.720
They've got guns
with night-scopes.

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:44.570
I wonder if they stole them from the armory, or took them from the hostages.

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:48.370
Illegal channels are
another possibility.

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:51.020
There's been a rumor of
that for some time, but...

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:52.500
This way !

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:53.530
I'm sure something moved.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:05:58.430
This is enough.

00:05:58.430 --> 00:05:59.310
Why don't we stop ?

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:01.200
What's enough ?

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.660
There might be enemies out here.

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:05.100
Let's stop here.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:07.050
It's impossible.

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:08.720
What ?!

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:11.590
Damn you ! You're
chickening out now ?

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:14.370
But it's impossible
to pull off a rebellion.

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:17.980
Rather than putting ourselves through this danger, if we just keep quiet...

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:20.950
...it's possible that we'll get
released in a prisoner exchange...

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:23.920
We don't know how long 
something like that could take !

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:24.860
But...

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:28.120
Hey, hey...

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:29.790
How could you understand ?

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:31.060
My family...

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:32.820
I'm an aristocrat !

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:35.330
I can't stand living
a poor life like this !

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:37.720
You're a commoner...

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:39.720
...so you're probably happy
in a dirty place like this !

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:42.470
But I'm different !

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:47.470
Why don't you cut it out ?

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:48.550
He's your fellow
countryman, isn't he ?

00:06:58.870 --> 00:06:59.870
Don't do that.

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:01.070
That hurts, you know.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:17.270
Nice job, Lieutenant.

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:20.300
Nah, he was just weak.

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:28.270
The Lieutenant must be able to
hew down 15 prisoners by himself.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:32.120
We'll ask these two
guys about the situation.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:33.600
So shall we retreat, for now ?

00:07:36.670 --> 00:07:38.170
Sounds like a good idea.{I agree.}

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:46.500
At 3:58, Yang and Patorichev returned to the
Central Control Room, via the Emergency Room.

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:50.810
They were able to gather some information
from the two prisoners, after they were treated.

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:57.390
So the leader of the rebellion
seems to be LTJG Presberg.

00:07:57.390 --> 00:08:01.660
They're saying that they'll release the other hostages if the Superintendent comes as a substitute.

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:04.820
Fool !

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:10.720
Was he criticizing
the prisoners, or me ?

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:14.290
What should we do ?

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:19.230
First, give me the
files on Presberg.

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:23.760
We've prepared them.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:30.480
An aristocratic brat, is he ?

00:08:32.390 --> 00:08:34.720
In a case like this, I guess
people wouldn't normally say...

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:38.450
"Oh, I'm impressed, he's
from an aristocratic family."

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:40.180
Lt. Commander Yang.

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:42.890
No, I mean Mr. Secretary.

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:45.120
This will be an important
decision for you.

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:47.890
Um, I am not quite
certain what you mean.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:53.960
If you make the wrong decision here, it might have an adverse impact on your future.

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:55.150
That's what I mean.

00:08:57.270 --> 00:09:02.560
In other words, he wants me to be the substitute hostage, in place of himself.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:04.230
What an obvious
threat he's making.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:07.980
Well, I wonder what
I'm supposed to do ?

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:14.930
I'm sure he can't say out loud that he wants
me to be the substitute hostage instead of him.

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:22.660
Lt. Commander Yang, you must
fulfill your duty as Secretary.

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:26.720
The prisoners are making
an outrageous demand...

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:29.820
...and the Superintendent cannot
afford to be taken hostage.

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:31.470
Therefore...

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:34.360
You'll be the hostage.

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:36.220
How brave of you.

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:38.890
No...I mean...

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:41.800
I was just joking.

00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:46.050
I suppose I have no choice
but to be the substitute here.

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:50.360
I'll go with him.

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:57.640
Lieutenant, you don't
have to accompany me.

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:01.500
Well, you're an important
person to me, Lt. Commander.

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:02.760
Lieutenant...

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:09.720
Since you're the only person on Econia that I can defeat in three-dimensional chess.

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:16.590
Hey, hey.

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:19.920
Lt. Commander Yang and Lt. Patorichev
are being sent as substitutes.

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:20.820
What do you think ?

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:25.480
I guess the Superintendent is taking the
opportunity to get rid of two of his "eyesores."

00:10:26.420 --> 00:10:27.320
"Eyesores" ?

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:33.600
Lt. Patorichev is a physical eyesore, and
Lt. Commander Yang is a psychological eyesore.

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:35.470
Lt. Commander Yang
is an eyesore, too ?

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:39.230
You don't have much
imagination, do you ?

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:44.110
When the Superintendent was 21 years old,
he wasn't even a low ranked officer.

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:46.670
On the other hand, now there's
a 21 year old Lt. Commander here.

00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:47.920
I'm sure he's not
happy about it.

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:49.870
I guess that's what
it's about, isn't it ?

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:17.590
We won't kill you.

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:22.080
You're both valuable hostages.
And we won't torture you either.

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:25.330
We're servicemen from the
glorious Galactic Empire.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:26.410
That's quite admirable.

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:32.030
I know Lt. Patorichev.

00:11:32.030 --> 00:11:34.220
But the other guy, are you
actually a Lt. Commander ?

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:39.710
I can't believe he's older or
more highly ranked than I am.

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:42.400
Please look at
my badge of rank.

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:43.770
And my identification card, too.

00:11:44.210 --> 00:11:45.250
I was going to !

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:52.120
He's right.

00:11:53.720 --> 00:11:54.720
All right.

00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:56.970
Release the hostages.

00:11:57.620 --> 00:12:03.740
Teach the infidels of the republic that
soldiers of the Empire do not break promises.

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:13.200
Hey you, Secretary, what kind of battlefield accomplishments have you achieved ?

00:12:14.230 --> 00:12:16.120
If you've made Lt. Commander
at such a young age...

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:18.020
...you must have done something
extraordinary to deserve it.

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:19.360
Right ?

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:21.120
That's right.

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:23.120
Unlike your country...

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:26.060
...in our nation, there's no one who gets
promoted based on lineage or social status.

00:12:26.670 --> 00:12:27.640
Shut up !

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:28.690
I'm not talking to you.

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:36.710
I rescued civilians from a siege by
your fleet in a starzone called El Facil.

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:39.700
So you don't have an accomplishment like destroying a battleship...

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:43.660
...or annihilating an enemy
unit all by yourself ?

00:12:44.510 --> 00:12:47.180
I'd like to do something
like that in my lifetime.

00:12:50.690 --> 00:12:54.920
This "boy" seems to be a simple believer in heroic militarism.

00:12:55.930 --> 00:12:57.640
Sorry to disappoint you.

00:13:12.590 --> 00:13:14.510
I guess it'd be strange to
tell them, "Take care."

00:13:21.720 --> 00:13:23.560
Are they all the hostages
you were holding ?

00:13:23.560 --> 00:13:24.460
Yes.

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:30.690
Do you think we would do such a dishonest trick like liberating hostages little by little ?

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:33.170
No, that wasn't
what I meant.

00:13:34.190 --> 00:13:36.770
I was thinking there might be
someone among the prisoners...

00:13:36.770 --> 00:13:39.970
...who opposed your plan
and was held here, but...

00:13:39.970 --> 00:13:41.590
There's no one
like that here !

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:43.760
Those who opposed our
plan left here already !

00:13:44.130 --> 00:13:46.030
I don't need
any cowards here !

00:13:47.150 --> 00:13:49.020
Where's Captain Kefenhiller, then ?

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:09.050
So, now that you have us as hostages,
what do you plan to demand ?

00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:12.110
An intergalactic spaceship.

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:14.340
Where are you planning
to go with the spaceship ?

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:17.370
We'll return home, of course.

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:18.390
I see.

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:21.070
You certainly can't go there on foot.
You definitely need a spaceship.

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:25.960
If you're intending to insult a soldier
of the Galactic Empire, I won't forgive you.

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:28.890
I'm not trying to insult you in the least.

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:32.410
Is there someone among you who can pilot the spaceship ?

00:14:33.530 --> 00:14:34.840
We've got one.

00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:38.360
How about an engineer, a navigator, or a communications officer ?

00:14:39.550 --> 00:14:40.520
Those are...

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:43.630
What an honest man...

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:49.470
In addition to the spaceship, we also plan to demand about 50 crewmen...

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:52.960
...plus a 3 month
supply of food.

00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:54.480
Lt. Commander !

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:58.720
It seems we're worth
a spaceship, 50 crewmen...

00:14:58.720 --> 00:15:02.490
...and 3 months worth of
food, all by ourselves !

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:04.590
That sounds grand !

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:10.590
But I doubt even our lifetime salaries would equal the price of a spaceship, though.

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:14.570
I must say there's
something utterly wrong...

00:15:14.570 --> 00:15:17.150
...with the calculations in this 
economic proposal, don't you think ?

00:15:17.150 --> 00:15:18.060
Cut it out !

00:15:24.850 --> 00:15:28.100
Though he did declare that
he wouldn't torture us...

00:15:28.100 --> 00:15:31.690
...it's still remarkable that he didn't raise his hand at us despite his obvious anger.

00:15:31.690 --> 00:15:35.090
I wonder if that's the good
upbringing of an aristocrat...

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:38.760
But then again, there's the
rogue like the one before{i.e. the initial capture, who beat up on his countryman}...

00:15:38.760 --> 00:15:40.790
...so there must be all kinds
of aristocratic people...

00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:43.870
Such an indomitable spirit, eh ?

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:49.760
Even I would be impressed with that passion,
and feel like shouting "Long Live the Empire !"

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:54.380
If you weren't taken by the
passion, what would you think ?

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.020
Let's see...

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:57.080
As far as
I'm concerned...

00:15:57.080 --> 00:16:01.530
...I'd rather live in a society where I'm free to publicly denounce corrupt politicians...

00:16:01.530 --> 00:16:05.970
...than in one where I'd be tortured unless I praised the Emperor.

00:16:06.590 --> 00:16:07.960
"Publicly," huh ?

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:10.140
Though only in principle, of course{i.e. not necessarily in actuality}.

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:12.170
But that's more than enough.

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:17.520
If there's principle, we can use that as
our grounds to criticize the higher-ups.

00:16:17.520 --> 00:16:22.600
I don't trust people who belittle the "principle" from the start.

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:27.890
Sorry to be preachy.

00:16:28.150 --> 00:16:31.100
But that's what
I honestly believe.

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:34.570
Without such a belief, I wouldn't have
become a professional military officer.

00:16:35.770 --> 00:16:37.470
I think it's remarkable.

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:41.870
Lieutenant Patorichev has such
a firmly established perspective.

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:45.310
If I thought he's just a man
of brawn, I'd be misjudging him.

00:16:48.770 --> 00:16:52.890
In any case, do you think the
Superintendent will rescue us ?

00:16:54.260 --> 00:16:56.270
Well, I think he'll at
least make some effort.

00:16:57.200 --> 00:17:00.720
Since I've become a
famous man for some reason...

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:04.480
...if the Captain abandons us,
it'll affect his reputation.

00:17:06.860 --> 00:17:12.120
To have the greenhorn {i.e. Yang}go through a scary experience and then rescue him and make him feel indebted...

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:14.820
...proving the true competency of the man who worked his way up the ladder in the field.

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:15.820
I guess that's his plan.

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:20.060
Of course, that is if everything goes in
accordance with the Captain's plan, but...

00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:25.200
Who's there ?

00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:27.510
It's me.

00:17:41.650 --> 00:17:43.710
What do you want, Kefenhiller ?

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:51.440
You're a despicable existence !

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:52.770
What you're doing is...

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:55.620
"An action unbecoming to
an Imperial serviceman..."

00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:57.960
"...behavior unbecoming to an
Imperial aristocrat, right ?"

00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:16.590
An old man is willingly giving himself up to be a hostage.

00:18:16.590 --> 00:18:18.370
So don't be so angry.

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:21.770
We'll have time to
talk our hearts out later.

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:31.120
It seems you've also
willingly become a hostage.

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:32.570
How eccentric of you.

00:18:32.570 --> 00:18:35.150
Really, why are
you here, Captain ?

00:18:35.810 --> 00:18:38.500
I'm interested in
you as a person.

00:18:38.500 --> 00:18:42.810
I thought I'd offer you my grandmotherly care and help you out a little.

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:44.650
So you're going to help us ?

00:18:45.300 --> 00:18:47.720
I didn't say
I'd rescue you.

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:49.920
How could I, under
the circumstances ?

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:54.440
But I could tell you a couple
of "underlying" circumstances.

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:56.980
I'm grateful for
your instruction.

00:18:57.390 --> 00:19:00.700
The first thing you have to
know is Costea's intentions.

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:08.070
Superintendent Costea has been embezzling
camp funds over the past several years.

00:19:08.070 --> 00:19:12.520
It seems there's a tiny, gaping
black hole within the bank vault.

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:15.230
About how much ?

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:17.460
Let's see.

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:24.230
As far as I know, it's somewhere around 350,000 to 360,000 dinars, I think.

00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:25.580
That much ?

00:19:25.580 --> 00:19:32.050
When Costea retires, his retirement fund should amount to 300,000 dinars.

00:19:32.050 --> 00:19:37.810
Costea's got a talent for money marketing so much so, that it's really a shame that he's in the military.

00:19:37.810 --> 00:19:38.870
Is there any proof ?

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:39.880
You're being noisy !

00:19:40.890 --> 00:19:42.650
You're all hostages !

00:19:42.650 --> 00:19:44.740
Just follow proper hostage etiquette.

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:47.260
"Proper hostage etiquette," eh ?

00:19:48.070 --> 00:19:52.470
Come to think of it, why isn't
Presberg making any moves ?

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:57.770
It appears as though he's been waiting for something, for some time.

00:19:57.770 --> 00:20:04.020
By the way, Captain, what kind of role am I supposed to play in this drama ?

00:20:04.020 --> 00:20:08.700
As was the case at El Facil, you, Lt. Commander Yang, are destined to be a hero on Econia, too.

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:11.230
But a dead one, of course.

00:20:12.710 --> 00:20:13.600
Not good...

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:16.100
I guess I'll get a true double-promotion this time around.

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:21.530
El Facil and Econia - their only common point is that both names start with an E, but...

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:25.030
Am I going to be a hero too,
along with Lt. Commander Yang ?

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:28.620
Unfortunately, Lieutenant,
you won't be a hero.

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:31.500
You've been given another role.

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:38.400
Lt. Patorichev will be responsible for the black hole in the bank vault, correct ?

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:43.720
I guess I'm not too
happy about that.

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:50.070
I'd rather not have an epitaph like "Public Funds Embezzler, Fyodor Patorichev, rests in peace here."

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:56.570
In a large society, there's large injustices,
and in a small society, there's small injustices.

00:20:57.270 --> 00:21:01.770
Even on a tiny internment camp planet like this, as long as positions of power exist...

00:21:01.770 --> 00:21:05.200
...they will start rotting from
the time of their inception.

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:08.680
This escape attempt is truly
impulsive and unsophisticated.

00:21:09.430 --> 00:21:13.430
But that's only how it seems on the surface, and underneath it, there might be...

00:21:14.090 --> 00:21:16.470
By the way, the things we
talked about last night...

00:21:16.470 --> 00:21:22.120
...Siegmeister and Michaelsen,
those two admirals...

00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:26.350
...there is one bridge that
connects these two affairs.

00:21:26.350 --> 00:21:28.530
That's what you
discovered, Captain ?

00:21:29.700 --> 00:21:32.760
I believe I found
out what was hidden.

00:21:35.400 --> 00:21:38.570
But in the end,
it's an Imperial affair.

00:21:38.570 --> 00:21:40.930
For me personally,
it's none of my business.

00:21:43.270 --> 00:21:46.810
Then how about Admiral Bruce Ashbey's possible murder ?

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:47.900
Eh ?

00:21:47.900 --> 00:21:50.230
I'm sure you're
very interested in this.

00:21:53.720 --> 00:21:55.200
I give up.

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:57.260
Captain, could you tell
me what you know ?

00:21:58.030 --> 00:22:02.200
A large-scale conspiracy that crosses both the Galactic Empire and the Free Planets Alliance.

00:22:03.230 --> 00:22:04.720
If it were a TV drama...

00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:08.400
...I'd title it "A Conspiracy Across Ten
Thousand Light Years" or something like that.

00:22:09.640 --> 00:22:16.320
Such a large-scale conspiracy, how would you be able to uncover it in a rural place like this ?

00:22:16.320 --> 00:22:18.640
Besides, it's something that
happened many decades ago.

00:22:19.620 --> 00:22:21.450
Time and place don't matter.

00:22:21.450 --> 00:22:24.720
If you have some information
and solid analytical ability...

00:22:24.720 --> 00:22:26.910
...you'll be able
to see the truth.

00:22:26.910 --> 00:22:29.620
More clearly than the parties
involved in the affair would.

00:22:34.720 --> 00:22:37.390
He's being played as a
mere puppet, I suppose ?

00:22:39.720 --> 00:22:42.670
I presume it was you who sent
the letters to the military offices...

00:22:42.670 --> 00:22:46.120
...claiming that Admiral Bruce
Ashbey's death was a murder plot ?

00:22:49.820 --> 00:22:50.690
Yes.

00:22:53.320 --> 00:22:55.290
It was a sudden attack.

00:22:55.980 --> 00:22:58.720
Merely two months after
the escape from El Facil...

00:22:58.720 --> 00:23:02.920
...Yang Wenli was once again
facing a threat to his life.

00:23:01.520 --> 00:23:04.200
Prisoners and Hostages

00:23:05.960 --> 00:23:09.850
[ Our Trail ]

00:23:05.960 --> 00:23:09.850
